### Describe the feature

Hi! Thanks for the useful library :)

I'm writing a CLI where most commands basically take a single argument with a few well-known options. The UX of these commands is better with a `positional` argument (so users don't have to write the arg name for no reason), but then it's missing all the goodies of an `enum` argument.

While consumers can work around this by implementing validation etc. themselves (which will also become easier if #103 is implemented), new argument types added in the future could also profit from being definable as positional/non-positional.

IMO making `positional` a boolean would make sense, something like this:

```diff
type _ArgDef<T extends ArgType, VT extends boolean | number | string> = {
  type?: T;
  description?: string;
  valueHint?: string;
-  alias?: string | string[];
  default?: VT;
  required?: boolean;
  options?: string[];
- };
+} & ({
+  alias?: string | string[];
+  positional?: false;
+} | {
+  positional: true;
+});
```

AFAICS this would mean `positional` arguments could be implemented as positional `string` arguments instead.

